hk: enable VK_EXT_memory_budget

Mesa !40238 (Christian Gmeiner, open since 2026-03-05). Honeykrisp has
implemented the budget query from the start, tracking every allocation
per heap and offering 90 % of what is free, but never advertised the
extension. Without it DXVK and vkd3d-proton can only go by the heap size,
not by what the rest of the system is using.

diff --git a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_physical_device.c b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_physical_device.c
index cc5fd0f..b98af06 100644
--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_physical_device.c
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ hk_get_device_extensions(const struct hk_instance *instance,
       .EXT_line_rasterization = true,
       .EXT_load_store_op_none = true,
       .EXT_map_memory_placed = true,
-      .EXT_memory_budget = false,
+      .EXT_memory_budget = true,
       .EXT_multi_draw = true,
       .EXT_mutable_descriptor_type = true,
       .EXT_non_seamless_cube_map = true,
